# ⚠️ Common Mistakes

## Mistake 1

> SYN means connection established.

❌ Wrong.

SYN starts connection establishment.

---

## Mistake 2

> SYN-ACK means connection is fully established.

❌ Not yet.

The client still needs to send the final ACK.

---

## Mistake 3

> ACK always means application data was received.

❌ Not necessarily.

TCP ACKs acknowledge TCP sequence information/bytes according to TCP's acknowledgement rules.

---

## Mistake 4

> Sequence number means packet number.

❌ Incorrect.

TCP sequence numbers track positions in the byte stream.

---

## Mistake 5

> HTTP handles TCP packet retransmission.

❌ Wrong.

TCP handles transport-level retransmission.

---

## Mistake 6

> Timeout means the server is definitely down.

❌ Not necessarily.

Firewall, routing, wrong port, packet loss, congestion, or an overloaded system can also cause timeouts.

