# 📖 Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| TCP | Connection-oriented transport protocol |
| SYN | Synchronize flag used to initiate connection |
| ACK | Acknowledgement |
| SYN-ACK | Server's SYN + acknowledgement of client's SYN |
| ISN | Initial Sequence Number |
| Sequence Number | Tracks position in TCP byte stream |
| Retransmission | Sending data again after loss |
| Timeout | Waiting period exceeded without expected response |
| RST | TCP Reset used to reject or reset a connection |
| TCP Handshake | Process of establishing a TCP connection |

